# 低频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List03核心词汇

cooperative /kəʊˈɒpərətɪv/ adj. 合作的 The project requires a cooperative approach. 该项目需要合作的方式。
cornerstone /ˈkɔːnəstəʊn/ n. 基石 Trust is the cornerstone of any relationship. 信任是任何关系的基石。
correlation /ˌkɒrəˈleɪʃn/ n. 关联 There is a strong correlation between education and income. 教育和收入之间有很强的关联性。
counteract /ˌkaʊntərˈækt/ v. 抵消 The new measures counteract the negative effects. 新措施抵消了负面影响。
counterfeit /ˈkaʊntəfɪt/ adj./v. 伪造 The police seized counterfeit goods worth millions. 警方查获了价值数百万的假冒商品。
covert /ˈkʌvət/ adj. 秘密的 The agency carried out covert surveillance. 该机构进行了秘密监视。
credentials /krɪˈdenʃlz/ n. 资质 She has excellent academic credentials. 她拥有优秀的学术资质。
curtail /kɜːˈteɪl/ v. 削减 The government curtailed public spending. 政府削减了公共开支。
cynical /ˈsɪnɪkl/ adj. 愤世嫉俗的 The public has become increasingly cynical about politics. 公众对政治越来越愤世嫉俗。
daunting /ˈdɔːntɪŋ/ adj. 令人畏惧的 The challenge is daunting but not insurmountable. 挑战令人畏惧但并非不可克服。
debut /ˈdeɪbjuː/ n./v. 首演 The product made its debut at the trade fair. 该产品在贸易博览会上首次亮相。
decay /dɪˈkeɪ/ v./n. 衰退 The old building has fallen into decay. 这座旧建筑已经衰败了。
deceive /dɪˈsiːv/ v. 欺骗 The advertisement was designed to deceive consumers. 该广告旨在欺骗消费者。
decree /dɪˈkriː/ n./v. 法令 The court issued a decree ordering the demolition. 法院下达了拆除令。
defect /ˈdiːfekt/ n./v. 缺陷 A design defect was discovered in the product. 产品中发现了设计缺陷。
defy /dɪˈfaɪ/ v. 违抗 The protesters defied the government's ban. 抗议者违抗了政府的禁令。
denounce /dɪˈnaʊns/ v. 公开谴责 The organization denounced the use of chemical weapons. 该组织公开谴责了化学武器的使用。
depict /dɪˈpɪkt/ v. 刻画 The film depicts the harsh realities of war. 这部电影刻画了战争的残酷现实。
deplete /dɪˈpliːt/ v. 耗尽 Overfishing has severely depleted fish stocks. 过度捕捞严重耗尽了鱼类资源。
deploy /dɪˈplɔɪ/ v. 调度 The company deployed additional resources to the project. 公司向项目调派了额外资源。
deprecate /ˈdeprɪkeɪt/ v. 反对 Critics deprecated the decision as short-sighted. 批评者反对这一决定，认为它目光短浅。
designate /ˈdezɪɡneɪt/ v. 指定 The building was designated as a heritage site. 该建筑被指定为遗产地。
desolate /ˈdesələt/ adj. 荒凉的 The village looked desolate after the evacuation. 疏散后，村庄看起来很荒凉。
devise /dɪˈvaɪz/ v. 设计 The team devised an innovative solution. 团队设计了一个创新的解决方案。
dignity /ˈdɪɡnəti/ n. 尊严 The constitution guarantees human dignity. 宪法保障人的尊严。
dilute /daɪˈluːt/ v. 稀释 The proposal dilutes the original standards. 该提案稀释了原始标准。
discern /dɪˈsɜːn/ v. 辨别 It is hard to discern the truth from the rumors. 很难从谣言中辨别真相。
discourse /ˈdɪskɔːs/ n. 话语 Public discourse on the issue has intensified. 关于该问题的公共话语已经加剧。
disperse /dɪˈspɜːs/ v. 散布 Seeds are dispersed by wind and water. 种子通过风和水散布。
disposition /ˌdɪspəˈzɪʃn/ n. 倾向 She has a natural disposition towards leadership. 她有天生的领导倾向。
